@abstract:
Declared intent and purpose for Neurophone.
@end

## Purpose

Neurophone is a neurosymbolic AI application for mobile devices.

It combines spiking neural networks (LSM + ESN) with local large language
models (Llama 3.2 via llama.cpp) and cloud fallback (Claude API) to deliver
on-device intelligence from phone sensor data.

Primary use case: real-time interpretation of phone sensor readings
(accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer, light, proximity) via a neural
pipeline, answerable in natural language.

Primary target: Android (Oppo Reno 13, Dimensity 8350). Long-term
cross-platform via gossamer (estate shell).

## In Scope

- Rust/Spark crates: lsm, esn, bridge, sensors, llm, claude-client,
  neurophone-core, neurophone-android
- Android application shell (Kotlin, migration to gossamer in progress)
- Proof corpus for neural-state invariants and lifecycle safety
- AI-assisted installation tooling
- Estate compliance (RSR, language-policy, governance, hypatia)

## Anti-Purpose

This project is NOT:
- A library (it is an application — for the routing library see heterogenous-mobile-computing)
- A monorepo for unrelated tools
- A fork or wrapper around an upstream project
- A cloud-first application (sensor data stays on device)

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask the owner.

Sensitive areas:
- ABI definitions in crates/neurophone-android/ (JNI contract)
- SPDX/licence headers (must be MPL-2.0)
- CI workflows in .github/workflows/ (only for compliance or directed changes)
- Owner-territory: PALIMPSEST.adoc, citation blocks, governance philosophy docs
- Proof corpus in proofs/ (add freely; do not delete existing)
- The gossamer migration path (do not substitute Tauri/Dioxus)
